# The tenth battle (stage 9) won by play, from the original's save after
# stage 8. The scene wins once the lance leader (unit 0) and the APC (unit 8)
# both stand on the gate's four cells (columns 194-195, rows 98-99); it is
# lost at 12:00 or if either of them is out of action. Hands-off nothing wins
# it: the enemies (12-13 and 16-19) march down the road and park on and by
# the gate, and the lance waits in the road's corridor at its start.
# The map (MAP3): the forest between the start and the east half leaves two
# ways through, the open strip along the top (rows 0-13) and the road's
# corridor (columns 141-144) up to its crossing at 146,57; south of the
# crossing the east half is open but for a lake (rows 70-93, columns 177-190)
# that the leader, a tank, cannot cross. So the APC's lance goes east along
# the top strip and down the open east half; the leader goes up the corridor
# to the crossing once the enemy column has passed it (10:38), and its three
# followers (F2-F4), their fire mode set to fire on any enemy, are each sent
# through the crossing once they reach the corridor. The lance then meets the
# enemies coming out from the gate (all destroyed by 10:45); the leader goes
# round the lake to the west and onto 194,99, and the APC onto 195,98 (its
# first stop is a cell short). Each unit is ordered on its own: a lance
# order keeps the leader's formation, and the corridor jams. Every order is
# given while the battle waits (a unit's commands are up); the keys that
# land in the running battle wait for a step (steps:1), and a message is
# answered with no idle after it.
# Then the menu over the battle: Save & Continue to slot 1: the save is
# REVENGE_SAVE_STAGE_09.
# set: campaign
# start-save: REVENGE_SAVE_STAGE_08
# Load Game, slot 1; the transmission; the battle (10:36:02).
idle:1000 Return idle:50 Right idle:50 Return idle:300 @snap:stage9_loaded
Return idle:600 @snap:stage9_transmission
Return steps:2 @snap:stage9_battle
